Database migrations for the Genkei Capital research-desk.

Conventions (see docs/storage.md):

- Hand-written only — autogenerate is disabled in env.py.
- File naming: YYYYMMDD_<slug>.py (date prefix sorts naturally).
- Connection URL comes from GENKEI_DATABASE_URL.
- Every migration must implement downgrade() or raise NotImplementedError
  with a comment explaining why a downgrade is impossible.
- TimescaleDB-specific objects (CREATE EXTENSION, hypertables, continuous
  aggregates) live in their own migrations, separate from base table DDL.

Common commands:

    GENKEI_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://... alembic upgrade head
    GENKEI_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://... alembic downgrade -1
    alembic revision -m "<short slug>"      # create a new (empty) migration
    alembic history                          # show all revisions
